\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Comparison of representative approaches related to vergence and accommodation sensing. Method denotes the primary sensing principle or eye representation, while Estimator denotes the strategy used to infer the target quantity. V/A Target specifies whether accommodation (A), vergence (V), both, or neither are directly estimated in the reported work. Near-eye indicates whether the method is demonstrated in a physical near-eye configuration. Green indicates favorable suitability for compact joint vergence--accommodation tracking, yellow indicates moderate suitability, and red indicates limited suitability. }}{2}{table.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
