\newlabel{tab:literature_review}{{1}{2}{Comparison of representative approaches related to vergence and accommodation sensing. Method denotes the primary sensing principle or eye representation, while Estimator denotes the strategy used to infer the target quantity. V/A Target specifies whether accommodation (A), vergence (V), both, or neither are directly estimated in the reported work. Near-eye indicates whether the method is demonstrated in a physical near-eye configuration. Green indicates favorable suitability for compact joint vergence--accommodation tracking, yellow indicates moderate suitability, and red indicates limited suitability}{table.caption.5}{}}
